begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 1 & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "ac2d41b9-a4e0-5932-86c4-15e0dad75b43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72a93e15-0e84-5909-858e-fec0bdb52b9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275545/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-275545/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "b614554d-78c7-5719-84f0-2ac8323e9ae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8896f6db-7a76-5b65-aada-105e4764b093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275545/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-275545/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0dc8a61d-1f90-5e4e-b095-be6b49220c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ff15f0d-fe61-5968-a359-ac65bdaaa19a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275545/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-275545/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-4/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "fa11b16b-97c4-50a8-ab20-72dc4e169227" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "60b7f9ce-fd8e-5296-9735-8167f1478869" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275545/field-4/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-275545/field-4/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275545" :question/id #uuid "3fcccfc3-31e7-59c0-8f2e-f8a8dc4379d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275545" :question/problem "If\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=2\\cdot -2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,6=2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,2=-1\\cdot -2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275545/field-1" "q-275545/field-2" "q-275545/field-3" "q-275545/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4406"] :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/1a753977affc5cc3dda18c9206116e1132254bccebd1e3f2545bea75bcc38f18.png)\nand \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/b99016bca94adc5de11eddef950fa13fc4349aaf95387468d07f294c409d029d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/64b831a66cdd9a3176d1eb916dfae189b41eb1f0f3ed3184797f92e404957878.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4407"] :question/problem "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/c6c7e580cfd96bc23c55742535ceb40a94635c2a44b911e0d08311c3a599c2fa.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
